e must be discarded or in use, but from previous history.\n\nPrevious player played B4, meaning they discarded B4. And unshown shows B4:3, which is consistent because if one was discarded, 4-1=3 left.\n\nSimilarly, F3: unshown is 3, and I have one F3, so total 4, minus mine, 3 unseen.\n\nF3 unshown:3, and I have F3:1, so yes.\n\nAlso, player across played F3, so they discarded F3, but F3 unshown is 3, which might include that or not? Let's see.\n\nGame history:\n\n- Across player: Play F3 \u2192 so they discarded F3\n\n- Previous player: Play B4 \u2192 discarded B4\n\nAnd unshown F3:3, but since across played F3, that means one F3 is discarded, so total F3 tiles: 4, one discarded (by across), one in my hand, so 2 should be unshown? But unshown says F3:3, which is confusing.\n\nUnshown tiles list: F3:3\n\nBut total tiles per type: 4 each.\n\n- Across player played F3, so one F3 is discarded.\n\n- I have F3:1, so one in my hand.\n\nTherefore, unshown should be 4 - 1 (discarded) - 1 (my hand) = 2.\n\nBut unshown says F3:3, which is inconsistent.\n\nPerhaps \"unshown\" includes only tiles in the wall, not discarded tiles.\n\nIn Mahjong, discarded tiles are visible to all, so \"unshown\" likely means tiles still in the wall, not yet drawn.\n\nSo for F3:\n\n- Total: 4\n\n- Discarded: across player played F3, so one discarded.\n\n- In hands: I have one F3, and possibly others, but we don't know other players' hands except what's shown.\n\nThe unshown count should be total minus discarded minus in known hands.\n\nKnown hands: only mine is fully known, others are partially known from melds and histories, but melds are all empty for others, and histories show discards.\n\nDiscarded tiles:\n\n- Across player: Play F3 \u2192 discarded F3\n\n- Previous player: Play B4 \u2192 discarded B4\n\nAlso, my game history is empty, so no discards from me yet.\n\nNext player history empty.\n\nPlayer across history: Play F3\n\nPrevious player history: Play B4\n\nSo discarded tiles so far: F